<pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ia8e265cdb532c91a3420bbeb1c51b11b5e91b6f0" commit="e763f9f086e3ea382550e038efa4e4c7e4ba4eb5" commit_message="shill: simplify dependency injection to DeviceInfo  DeviceInfo depends on EventDispatcher, Metrics, and Manager. These dependencies are currently injected via the constructor of DeviceInfo. The same applies to all DeviceInfo subclasses. Manager also depends on EventDispatcher, and Metrics, which can conveniently serve as a &quot;context object&quot; for injecting and forwarding these dependencies to DeviceInfo. While explicit dependency injection is generally preferred as it avoids obscure or unnecessary coupling of dependencies, in case of DeviceInfo, forwarding additional dependencies via Manager substantially simplifies the code structure and also avoids DeviceInfo and Manager from using different dependencies in tests, which could lead to mismatches between the production environment and the test environment.  BUG=None TEST=Run unit tests.  Change-Id: Ia8e265cdb532c91a3420bbeb1c51b11b5e91b6f0 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/1650098 Commit-Ready: Ben Chan &lt;benchan@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Ben Chan &lt;benchan@chromium.org&gt; Legacy-Commit-Queue: Commit Bot &lt;commit-bot@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Hugo Benichi &lt;hugobenichi@google.com&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="1650098" owner_email="benchan@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform2" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform2" ref="refs/changes/98/1650098/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I62694becee1c001a6edb79d12f7d52bdc1d2f6ab" commit="8f6675764cfa96e98f5c2377024df98a7a760fae" commit_message="shill: cellular: simplify object access in Cellular  Cellular is derived from Device, which can already access its associated Manager, ControlInterface, EventDispatcher, and Metrics via the corresponding getters from Device. There is no need to go through ModemInfo, which will be refactored in a follow-up CL.  BUG=None TEST=Run unit tests.  Change-Id: I62694becee1c001a6edb79d12f7d52bdc1d2f6ab Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/1650099 Commit-Ready: Ben Chan &lt;benchan@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Ben Chan &lt;benchan@chromium.org&gt; Legacy-Commit-Queue: Commit Bot &lt;commit-bot@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Alex Khouderchah &lt;akhouderchah@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="1650099" owner_email="benchan@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform2" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform2" ref="refs/changes/99/1650099/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Id058bba3d486f4bf14f8e5be5c8c787c10511fb5" commit="2169050c4c7c89493007cf563dcf4bfc869e4836" commit_message="shill: cellular: remove CellularService's dependency on ModemInfo  ModemInfo will be refactored in a follow-up CL. CellularService doesn't really depend on ModemInfo as it only uses ModemInfo to obtain Manager for the Service's constructor. This CL updates CellularService's constructor to take a Manager instead of ModemInfo, which is consistent with other Service derived classes.  BUG=None TEST=Run unit tests.  Change-Id: Id058bba3d486f4bf14f8e5be5c8c787c10511fb5 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/1652362 Commit-Ready: Ben Chan &lt;benchan@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Ben Chan &lt;benchan@chromium.org&gt; Legacy-Commit-Queue: Commit Bot &lt;commit-bot@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Alex Khouderchah &lt;akhouderchah@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="1652362" owner_email="benchan@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform2" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform2" ref="refs/changes/62/1652362/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Iefcb83fed23